  "reason": "The completed experiments show a strong RNA-only baseline (config_001, acc 0.485, F1 0.464) but a weak image-only ResNet50 baseline (config_010, acc 0.208, F1 0.172). The key uncertainty is whether the image modality is intrinsically uninformative or simply poorly represented by ResNet50. config_013 tests a stronger image encoder, ImageNet ViT-L, while keeping the same image-only singleprofile setting, so it isolates the effect of image representation. This is the best next experiment because it determines whether an image branch is worth combining in multimodal models before spending limited budget on more complex fusion or multiprofile variants."
